# Grimnir operator-local hygiene patterns — TEMPLATE (ships clean; safe to track).
#
# Copy to  ~/.grimnir/hygiene-patterns.txt  (or point $GRIMNIR_HYGIENE_PATTERNS at
# it) and fill in YOUR identifiers. scripts/check-repo-hygiene.sh loads this list
# to catch operator-specific leakage the generic patterns deliberately don't —
# your hosts, IPs, email, and real program/client names.
#
# Keep the REAL file private (chmod 600); NEVER commit it. It lives outside the
# repo by default (~/.grimnir/), so there is nothing to gitignore.
#
# Format: one case-insensitive extended-regex (ERE) per line. Blank lines and
# lines beginning with # are ignored. Escape dots in literal IPs/emails (1\.2\.3\.4).
#
# ── Examples (replace with your own, then delete these) ──
# you@example\.com                       # operator email
# \b(host-a|host-b|host-c)\b             # your machine / VPS hostnames
# 203\.0\.113\.7                         # your home / office public IP
# 100\.64\.12\.34                        # your EXACT Tailscale (tailnet) IP
# \bAcmeCorp\b                           # a real client / program name (per engagement)
